  "note": "Trace form (research/trace-harness.md) for L01a's Prisma 7.10.1 twins, with @prisma/adapter-pg: run as they are against PostgreSQL, their tables made from each twin's prisma/schema.prisma by prisma migrate diff, the data from seed.sql at 1x and 10x. Each request is sent three times (a warm-up, then two measured), statements counted with pg_stat_statements. n is the items a request handles at 1x; items says where they are counted. The twins take at most 50 orders and customers and 100 invoices, so at 10x those requests handle 50 or 100 items, not 100: still more than five times as many. Decoys, in both twins: findUnique per order in Promise.all, which Prisma 7 sends as one query (research/probes/prisma7-batching); include; the customer-name helper once; three fixed settings; a batch $transaction of findUnique. GET /invoices is mounted on a router, so its route is given.",
